import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 307 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou: Solitary Dao vs. Symbiosis Ultimate Divide","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 307 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou: Solitary Dao vs. Symbiosis Ultimate Divide","no":307,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Ye Fan","Heng Yuan Zhou","Solitary Dao vs. Symbiosis","Ultimate Divide"],"related":["01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0307_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs衡元宙.md","filePath":"en/0307_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs衡元宙.md"}'),n={name:"en/0307_模块2-遮天-叶凡vs衡元宙.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,d,h){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-307-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-ye-fan-vs-heng-yuan-zhou-solitary-dao-vs-symbiosis-ultimate-divide" tabindex="-1">Entry 307 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou: Solitary Dao vs. Symbiosis Ultimate Divide <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-307-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-ye-fan-vs-heng-yuan-zhou-solitary-dao-vs-symbiosis-ultimate-divide" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 307 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou: Solitary Dao vs. Symbiosis Ultimate Divide&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 20) | Benchmark base: Documents 01, 03, 04</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-one-person-immortalizes-or-myriad-ranks-ascend-together" tabindex="-1">Introduction: One person immortalizes, or Myriad Ranks ascend together <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-one-person-immortalizes-or-myriad-ranks-ascend-together" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: One person immortalizes, or Myriad Ranks ascend together&quot;">​</a></h2><p>All six top-level axioms present; this entry does the ultimate contrast: Ye Fan represents &quot;solitary Dao&quot; — one person becomes emperor, Myriad Ranks look up; Heng Yuan Zhou represents &quot;symbiosis&quot; — Myriad Ranks republican, collectively ascend. This is not good-vs-evil, but a generation gap in civilization form. The law-first axiom requires: any &quot;solitary Dao&quot; narrative must answer &quot;what happens to Myriad Ranks after you leave.&quot; Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Solitary Dao vs. symbiosis energy-investment difference:</p><ul><li><strong>Ye Fan solitary Dao</strong>: cosmos-tier aptitude all invested in &quot;one person immortalizing,&quot; Myriad Ranks watching from the side</li><li><strong>Heng Yuan Zhou symbiosis</strong>: strong ones&#39; energy transmitted through the Anchor Network to Myriad Ranks; one breakthrough lifts a group</li></ul><p>The same power: solitary Dao makes all beings idle; symbiosis makes all beings ride the momentum. This is not a difference of power magnitude, but of power flow direction.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Solitary Dao&#39;s fundamental flaw:</p><ol><li><strong>Person leaves, Dao breaks</strong>: Ye Fan&#39;s Dao exists with him personally; he does not write it down, does not institutionalize it; later generations must re-grope</li><li><strong>Myriad Ranks no subjectivity</strong>: Ye Fan present = Myriad Ranks benefit; Ye Fan gone = Myriad Ranks adrift</li><li><strong>Solitary Dao = endpoint</strong>: solitary-Dao settings implicitly assume &quot;no second Ye Fan&quot;; civilization&#39;s ascending line caps at Ye Fan</li></ol><p>Symbiosis is the opposite: institutions present, Myriad Ranks self-iterate on the ascending line, no need to wait for the next Ye Fan.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Solitary-Dao narrative itself is the ultimate form of predatory thinking:</p><ul><li><strong>&quot;I walk for you&quot;</strong>: Ye Fan bears the evolution task Myriad Ranks should have jointly borne</li><li><strong>&quot;You just watch&quot;</strong>: Myriad Ranks are arranged as audience, losing practice-subject qualification</li><li><strong>&quot;My Dao need not be public&quot;</strong>: highest wisdom retained in one person / trusted line</li></ul><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s counter-question: Ye Fan walked for Myriad Ranks for a hundred thousand years; have Myriad Ranks themselves learned to walk? The answer is no.</p><p>Solitary Dao vs. symbiosis&#39;s ultimate divide can also be tested by one question: if the protagonist suddenly disappeared, would the world get better, worse, or unchanged? Gu Chensha disappears = world loses its engine; Tang Luo disappears = academy falls, universal-benefit breaks; Ye Fan disappears = dark turmoil recurs — all three get worse. In Heng Yuan Zhou any anchor disappears, the world runs as usual, because order has long been written into institutions and network. This &quot;disappearance test&quot; is Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s final touchstone for judging all Myriad-Realms civilizations. Ye Fan did the best solitary Dao in his era, but &quot;best solitary Dao&quot; is still solitary Dao — disappearance = collapse; this is its ceiling.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Ye Fan Solitary Dao</th><th>Heng Yuan Zhou Symbiosis</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One person becomes emperor</td><td>Myriad Ranks republican co-build</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad Ranks look up</td><td>Myriad Ranks co-build</td></tr><tr><td>Dao follows the person</td><td>Dao enters the Alaya whole-network</td></tr><tr><td>After Ye Fan leaves = turmoil</td><td>After any individual leaves = no effect</td></tr><tr><td>Civilization caps at Ye Fan</td><td>Civilization infinitely iterates</td></tr><tr><td>Solitary Dao</td><td>Symbiosis</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate solitary-Dao and symbiotic civilizations&#39; full evolution</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: simulate &quot;protagonist nirvana&quot; events in both worlds</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: civilization trajectory at 100-year, 1000-year, 10000-year scales</li><li><strong>Review</strong>: conclusion — solitary-Dao civilization enters oscillation after protagonist nirvana; symbiotic civilization continuously rises; after ten thousand years the gap is not comparable</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency</strong>: Ye Fan medium-low; Heng Yuan Zhou high</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: Ye Fan high; Heng Yuan Zhou zero</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: Ye Fan = medium; Heng Yuan Zhou = extremely low</li></ul><p>Solitary Dao vs. symbiosis also have an ultimate difference: solitary Dao&#39;s endpoint is &quot;I finally arrived&quot;; symbiosis&#39;s endpoint is &quot;we arrived together.&quot; Ye Fan becomes a Red-Dust Immortal; he personally reaches cultivation apex, but Myriad Ranks remain in place; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Origin Realm strong one, while reaching apex, his civilization as a whole rises one step. The former&#39;s &quot;arrival&quot; is lonely; the latter&#39;s &quot;arrival&quot; is collective. A novel can write one person&#39;s lonely summit, but a civilization cannot pin hope on such loneliness.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: solitary Dao makes Myriad Ranks idle; symbiosis lets Myriad Ranks ride momentum</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: solitary-Dao narrative itself takes evolution-subject qualification from Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least tried universal benefit; Ye Fan did not even do universal benefit — solitary Dao is colder than bestowal</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: symbiosis is the Myriad-Races axiom&#39;s direct realization</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: only symbiotic civilization qualifies to talk about cross-multiverse</li></ul><p>Solitary Dao vs. symbiosis also have a testable metric: what the strong one leaves behind is &quot;story&quot; or &quot;institution.&quot; Ye Fan leaves an exciting story; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s anchors leave a runnable institution. Stories are told for generations, but cannot stop turmoil; institutions are unexciting, but they can stop turmoil. What civilization ultimately needs is not excitement, but stability.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Ye Fan&#39;s Dao is his alone; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Dao is Myriad Ranks&#39; Dao. The former however exciting is one person&#39;s epic; the latter however plain is the entire cosmos&#39; daily life. Shrouding-the-Heavens wrote a good novel, but did not write a good civilization — because it pinned civilization&#39;s hope on one person&#39;s dantian.</p><p>Solitary Dao&#39;s end is one person&#39;s back; symbiosis&#39;s end is Myriad Ranks&#39; group photo. Ye Fan&#39;s back is tall enough, but Heng Yuan Zhou chooses the group photo — because the group photo has Myriad Ranks, while the back has only one person.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Ye Fan vs. Heng Yuan Zhou described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./288_模块2-遮天-总论叶凡孤道与寡头式文明.html">Entry 288 · Overview</a> · <a href="./308_模块2-遮天-锚点共生替代方案.html">Entry 308 · Anchor Symbiosis Alternative</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/01-锚点共生文明宣言.html">01-Anchor Symbiotic Civilization Manifesto</a></li></ul>',35)])])}const y=i(n,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,y as default};
